<BaseLayout title="About | Basim">
  <main>
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I'm Basim, a second-year Electrical Engineering undergraduate at UCLA. I am a member of UCLA's FSAE Electric Racing team, where I develop Low Voltage PCBs responsible for critical vehicle functions. I was previously at Tenstorrent where I wrote open-source software for TT's RISC-V AI hardware. I will be returning to Tenstorrent this summer on the scale-out team, contributing to multi-device HPC firmware. 
    </p>

    <p>
    This website is a portfolio of my technical projects/experience as well as an exhibit for some of my other hobbies.
    </p>

    <h3>Interests</h2>

    <p>
    I am interested in a multitude of electrical engineering subfields, including power electronics, PCB design, feedback control systems, digital design, low-level programming, and wireless systems.
    </p>

    <h3>Hobbies</h3>
    I like cars, planes, watches, comedy, photography, and traveling, and often spend my free time learning more about these topics.
  </main>
